     "design": {
      "purpose": "Change a fraction to a decimal by long division and tell whether it ends or repeats.",
      "principles": [
       "PRINCIPLE_SYSTEMATIC_VARIATION"
      ],
      "rationale": "Long division of the numerator by the denominator shows that a fraction's decimal either ends or repeats, which is what the standard asks a student to know. Some denominators are made only of 2s and 5s and end; others, such as 3, 11 and 15, repeat. There is room under each fraction for the long division.",
      "misconceptions": [
       "Dividing the denominator by the numerator.",
       "Thinking a fraction with a large denominator must repeat, such as 33/40."
      ]
     },
